            <ArticleTitle>The continuing legacy of nature versus nurture in biolinguistics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>140-141</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3758/s13423-016-1202-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Theories of language evolution that separate biological and cultural contributions perpetuate a false dichotomy between nature and nurture. The explanatory power of future theories will depend on acknowledging the reality of gene-culture interaction and how it makes language possible.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
